{
  "schema": "spec@1",
  "id": "SPEC-002",
  "purpose": "Make [[package]] rule lookup specificity-ordered so a prefixed pattern (cargo:foo) always wins over a bare pattern (foo) regardless of TOML declaration order, and emit a warning diagnostic when a bare rule matches packages in more than one ecosystem.",
  "scope": "Two changes in ManifestWalkResolver::build in crates/callisto-graph/src/walk.rs: (1) the [[package]] rule lookup on line ~154, and (2) a new cross-ecosystem diagnostic pass after the packages loop. One new DiagnosticCode variant added to crates/callisto-model/src/diagnostic.rs. PackageId::matches() is NOT changed.",
  "non_goals": [
    "PackageId::matches() in identity.rs: bare-matches-all-ecosystems is correct and intentional. The fix is at the call site, not in the type.",
    "[[package-set]] rules: multi-ecosystem glob matching is their explicit purpose; they are exempt from the cross-ecosystem diagnostic.",
    "Specificity ordering among multiple Prefixed matches with different ecosystems: first-match-wins (declaration order) is correct for that case.",
    "Specificity ordering among multiple Bare matches: first-match-wins (declaration order) is unchanged.",
    "No new E-code is added: the diagnostic is a Warning, not a miette-diagnosed Error."
  ],
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    {
      "id": "AC-1",
      "description": "When cfg.packages contains a Prefixed PackageId rule (ecosystem() is Some) and a Bare PackageId rule (ecosystem() is None) that both match the same package, the Prefixed rule's PackageConfig is applied to that package, regardless of which rule appears first in cfg.packages.",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-2",
      "description": "When cfg.packages contains only Bare PackageId rules that match the same package, the first-matching rule in declaration order is applied (existing behavior, unchanged).",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-3",
      "description": "When cfg.packages contains only Prefixed PackageId rules that match the same package, the first-matching rule in declaration order is applied.",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-4",
      "description": "When no [[package]] rule matches a package, the [[package-set]] fallback is still consulted. This existing behavior is unchanged.",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-5",
      "description": "When a Bare PackageId rule in cfg.packages matches packages from exactly two or more distinct ecosystems in the discovered workspace, exactly one Diagnostic is pushed to ManifestWalkResolver::diagnostics with: severity = Warning, code = DiagnosticCode::BareRuleMatchesMultipleEcosystems (new variant), and a message containing the pattern string and the matched ecosystem names.",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-6",
      "description": "When a Bare PackageId rule in cfg.packages matches packages from only one distinct ecosystem (or matches no packages at all), no diagnostic is pushed for that rule.",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-7",
      "description": "Prefixed PackageId rules in cfg.packages never trigger the cross-ecosystem diagnostic regardless of what they match.",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-8",
      "description": "Rules in cfg.package_sets never trigger the cross-ecosystem diagnostic regardless of what they match.",
      "is_error_case": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-9",
      "description": "When cfg.packages is empty, no diagnostic is pushed and rule lookup returns None for every package. This empty-input case is not an error.",
      "is_error_case": false
    }
  ],
  "api_surface": {
    "file": "crates/callisto-graph/src/walk.rs",
    "changes": [
      "Replace the cfg.packages.iter().find(...) call (the [[package]] lookup, ~line 154) with a two-pass search: first pass finds any Prefixed-pattern match (pattern.ecosystem().is_some()); second pass (only if first is None) finds any Bare-pattern match. Both passes use first-match-wins within their tier. Result is the same Option<&PackageConfig> type as before.",
      "After the packages loop (after packages.insert), add a pass over cfg.packages: for each (pattern, _) where pattern.ecosystem().is_none() (Bare), collect the distinct ecosystems of all packages in the just-built packages map whose id is matched by pattern. If the ecosystem count is > 1, push one Diagnostic { code: DiagnosticCode::BareRuleMatchesMultipleEcosystems, severity: DiagnosticSeverity::Warning, message: format!(...), package: None, path: None, .. }."
    ],
    "new_variants": [
      "DiagnosticCode::BareRuleMatchesMultipleEcosystems in crates/callisto-model/src/diagnostic.rs — add to the end of the DiagnosticCode enum, kebab-case serde name 'bare-rule-matches-multiple-ecosystems'."
    ]
  }
}

